# boxhuman — the crowd goes over and comes back. H no longer snaps a figure
# upside down: the five steps that derive the handstand pose are taken IN TIME
# instead of all at once, so the arms come up, the body turns over about the
# hips, the legs open into the straddle and the palms turn down to meet the
# floor. Each build's SPEED comes off its own stiffness (the bruiser snaps over
# in 32 frames, the kid takes 57) and the starts are staggered, so what you
# watch is a wave rolling down the line.
down  40 H
up    43 H
down 260 H
up   263 H
